stores elements from some total order, so that any two elements \ensuremath{\ensuremath{\ensuremath{\mathit{x}}}}
and \ensuremath{\ensuremath{\ensuremath{\mathit{y}}}} can be compared.  In code examples, this will be done with a
method called \ensuremath{\ensuremath{\mathrm{compare}(\ensuremath{\mathit{x}},\ensuremath{\mathit{y}})}} in which

